    "semantics": "tsOutput = the CURRENT TS scrubber's byte-for-byte output when the upstream stream is cut at byte splitAtByte (two chunks): the scrubber decodes+scrubs EACH CHUNK INDEPENDENTLY, so a tag straddling the boundary is not recognized (its halves leak through) and an unterminated block only drops the remainder OF ITS OWN CHUNK. expectedRust = single-pass scrub of the whole stream (atomic model): a split tag is still removed; an unterminated block drops everything from the open tag onward. Rust must reproduce expectedRust for ALL splits.",
